// bowl.mat — VM-091 (unified-engine migration Task 2). The camera bowl's
// material: per-fragment sampling (Decision resolution 2, 2026-09-11) of up
// to kMaxBowlCameras (6) camera textures, matching reproject.cu's bowl_kernel
// per-camera loop (right/down/fwd/t projection, plumb_bob distortion, border
// feather x alignment^2 weight) as closely as a rasterizer material can.
//
// UNLIT: the bowl's color IS the camera pixels, same rationale as
// point_cloud.mat/trajectory_carpet.mat -- PBR shading would add a
// light-direction term nobody asked for.
//
// The interpolant budget (MATERIAL_VARIABLES_COUNT = 4, Decision 3) holds
// TWO custom vec4s here, well inside budget:
//   CUSTOM0 (via `requires: [ color ]`, vertex passes material.color
//     through) = {coverage_a, index_a, coverage_b, index_b} -- the per-vertex
//     bake's output (bowl_mesh.cpp). index_a/index_b are LITERALLY IDENTICAL
//     across a triangle's three vertices by construction (Decision 3's
//     per-triangle-uniform-index rule), so linearly interpolating them
//     reproduces the same integer everywhere in the triangle -- safe to
//     round-trip through int(x + 0.5) in the fragment shader.
//   CUSTOM2 (via `requires: [ custom0 ]`, a real vertex attribute, NOT
//     packed through uv0/uv1 -- see the review-round-1 note below) = the
//     vertex's RIG-FRAME position (bowl_mesh.cpp bakes/generates positions
//     in rig frame -- Decision 3's frame convention). This is NOT the same
//     as Filament's own getWorldPosition(): the bowl entity's
//     TransformManager transform is the map<-rig ego pose (renderer.cpp's
//     update_bowl, matching update_ego_transform), so getWorldPosition()
//     would be MAP frame -- wrong frame for camera extrinsics, which are
//     rig-frame (scene.h). Carrying rig-frame position as its own
//     interpolant is what makes "per-fragment sampling from the rasterized
//     [rig-frame] position" (Decision resolution 2) mean the position is
//     interpolated PER FRAGMENT across the triangle (much finer than the
//     per-vertex bake this decision replaced), not merely read once per
//     vertex.
//
// REVIEW ROUND 1 (2026-09-11) BLOCKING FINDING -- rigPos does NOT ride
// uv0/uv1 anymore: Filament's generated vertex shader V-FLIPS both
// (`vec2(mesh_uv0.x, 1.0 - mesh_uv0.y)`, confirmed via
// `matc -a opengl -p desktop -o /tmp/bowl.filamat bowl.mat && matinfo
// --print-glsl=0 /tmp/bowl.filamat`) -- correct for an actual texture UV,
// silently corrupting for a position payload smuggled through the same
// channel (every fragment sampled from (x, 1-y, z) instead of (x, y, z),
// wrong everywhere y != 0.5). rigPos now rides a REAL custom vertex
// attribute instead: `filament::VertexAttribute::CUSTOM0` (FLOAT3, bound in
// bowl.cpp's make_bowl_vertex_buffer), requested here via `requires: [
// custom0 ]` and read with `getCustom0()` in materialVertex -- Filament
// passes CUSTOM attributes through with no per-component arithmetic. It is
// then carried across the rasterizer on its own interpolant, `custom2`
// (custom1 is not declared -- nothing uses it), exactly like weight/index
// use custom0.
//
// PARAMETER BUDGET, empirically discovered, not assumed: this matc build
// (1.56.5) aborts with "Too many parameters" past a per-material uniform
// float-count ceiling well below what MAX_SAMPLER_COUNT/interpolant-budget
// math alone would predict (verified experimentally: a material with 6
// cameras' full right/down/fwd/t + K + dist(4) + widthHeightK3(4) [24
// floats/camera, 148 total] aborts; 5 cameras at that footprint [124 total]
// does not). This material is therefore deliberately trimmed to 18
// floats/camera (108 total + 6 shared = 114):
//   - Per-camera parameters are 6 SEPARATELY NAMED uniforms each (camRightN/
//     camFwdN/camTN/camKN/camDistN/camK3_N/camTexN), not a `size:`-declared
//     array: this matc build does not correctly support array-typed
//     material parameters at all (verified separately -- a
//     `{ type: float4, name: arr, size: 6 }` parameter compiles, but
//     `materialParams.arr[i]` type-checks as a scalar float / single-vec4
//     access, not an array index, for both constant and dynamic indices).
//     This also sidesteps a real hazard the plan names for a SAMPLER
//     array: selecting a sampler by a fragment-computed index is
//     non-dynamically-uniform sampler indexing (illegal/UB in GLSL) -- the
//     fragment shader below instead unrolls a static (compile-time-
//     constant) per-camera block for each of the 6 cameras, each gated by
//     a runtime equality check (`idxA == N`) against the baked index
//     rather than by indexing a sampler array, so no dynamic sampler
//     indexing ever occurs.
//   - NO per-camera `down` uniform: reconstructed in-shader as
//     cross(fwd, right) -- exact for an orthonormal right-handed basis
//     (which right/down/fwd always are, being columns of a rotation
//     matrix), not an approximation.
//   - NO per-camera width/height uniform: read via textureSize() on the
//     already-bound camera texture, which is exactly the camera's real
//     pixel dimensions (BowlConfig's cam_width/cam_height are what sized
//     the texture in the first place, camera_textures.cpp).
//   - NO per-camera mat4 ego-motion-delta uniform: an earlier draft
//     carried one (Task 1's set_camera_motion_delta), but composing it
//     into the EFFECTIVE right/fwd/t above on the CPU (bowl.cpp's
//     update_bowl, once per render_frame call -- a 3x3 transpose-multiply
//     per camera, no matrix inverse needed since an ego-motion delta's
//     rotation is orthonormal) is both well inside this budget and
//     cheaper than a GPU-side mat4 multiply per fragment would have been.
//
// REVIEW ROUND 1 BLOCKING FINDING -- border feather is now computed
// PER-FRAGMENT, from a new `featherMargin` parameter (bowl.cpp pushes
// BowlConfig::feather_margin), ported verbatim from blend.cuh's
// border_feather/smoothstep01 at the fragment's own xp/yp. It used to be
// baked per-vertex into coverage_a/coverage_b, which does not match a
// per-fragment-sampled UV: the fragment hard-rejects at `xp > width-1`
// carrying the full interpolated vertex weight right up to that line,
// turning each camera's image edge into a step instead of the smoothstep
// feather reproject.cu produces. coverage_a/coverage_b (bowl_mesh.cpp) now
// carry ONLY the alignment^2 term (renamed from weight_a/weight_b).
//
// REVIEW ROUND 1 MINOR FINDING -- texture UV is pixel-CENTER sampled
// (`(xp,yp) + 0.5`), not pixel-CORNER (`xp/width`): matches GL's own texel
// center convention and reproject.cu's `bilinear()`, which samples at xp
// exactly. `bowl_projection.cpp`'s `ProjectToCameraUv` keeps its own
// pixel-CORNER convention (its header comment states this explicitly) --
// this +0.5 is applied here, shader-side, only, converting xp/yp (which
// bowl_mesh.cpp already derives as `u*width`/`v*height`) back to a
// pixel-center-sampled UV.
//
// skyColor mirrors BowlConfig's own sky_color field -- bowl.cpp pushes it
// once per set_bowl_config() call.
//
// REVIEW ROUND 1 MINOR FINDING -- exposureCompensation is now a material
// PARAMETER (BowlConfig::exposure_compensation, default 10.0, bowl.cpp
// pushes it), not a hardcoded shader constant: a style knob alongside
// sky_color/feather_margin, per the STANDING "every rendered element ships
// style tokens" directive. It intentionally does NOT multiply skyColor
// (see the fragment code below) -- sky_color is authored already in
// display/post-tonemap space (what a user picks in a color swatch), not in
// the same pre-tonemap space sampled camera pixels live in, so multiplying
// it by exposureCompensation would make any sky_color above ~0.1 clip to
// white for no reason a user configuring sky_color would expect.
//
// REVIEW ROUND 1 MINOR FINDING -- this material contributes at most 2
// cameras per fragment (CUSTOM0/CUSTOM2 are both spoken for: weight/index
// and rigPos), and the top-2 pair is chosen PER TRIANGLE (bowl_mesh.cpp),
// so across a triple-camera-overlap band adjacent triangles can switch
// from blending (A,B) to (A,C) at equal summed weight -- a mesh-aligned
// faceted seam reproject.cu's all-camera blend does not have. Recorded as
// a NAMED PARITY EXCEPTION (Task 4 Step 1's checklist, migration plan doc)
// rather than fixed here -- test_bowl.cpp's
// ThreeCameraOverlapStillPicksAConsistentPairPerTriangle documents the
// current (2-camera) behavior at a real triple-overlap triangle so a
// future fix has a test to change deliberately, not silently.
//
// OPAQUE (no `blending:` line -- Filament's default): the STANDING
// opaque-while-fresh convention (ribbon_emissive.mat's header) applies here
// too -- the bowl is either fully covered (alpha 1, some camera contributed)
// or shows sky_color (also alpha 1); it is never a blended/translucent
// surface, so it must never sit in Filament's blended queue.
material {
    name : bowl,
    shadingModel : unlit,
    parameters : [
        { type : sampler2d, name : camTex0 },
        { type : sampler2d, name : camTex1 },
        { type : sampler2d, name : camTex2 },
        { type : sampler2d, name : camTex3 },
        { type : sampler2d, name : camTex4 },
        { type : sampler2d, name : camTex5 },
        { type : float3, name : camRight0 },
        { type : float3, name : camFwd0 },
        { type : float3, name : camT0 },
        { type : float4, name : camK0 },
        { type : float4, name : camDist0 },
        { type : float, name : camK3_0 },
        { type : float3, name : camRight1 },
        { type : float3, name : camFwd1 },
        { type : float3, name : camT1 },
        { type : float4, name : camK1 },
        { type : float4, name : camDist1 },
        { type : float, name : camK3_1 },
        { type : float3, name : camRight2 },
        { type : float3, name : camFwd2 },
        { type : float3, name : camT2 },
        { type : float4, name : camK2 },
        { type : float4, name : camDist2 },
        { type : float, name : camK3_2 },
        { type : float3, name : camRight3 },
        { type : float3, name : camFwd3 },
        { type : float3, name : camT3 },
        { type : float4, name : camK3 },
        { type : float4, name : camDist3 },
        { type : float, name : camK3_3 },
        { type : float3, name : camRight4 },
        { type : float3, name : camFwd4 },
        { type : float3, name : camT4 },
        { type : float4, name : camK4 },
        { type : float4, name : camDist4 },
        { type : float, name : camK3_4 },
        { type : float3, name : camRight5 },
        { type : float3, name : camFwd5 },
        { type : float3, name : camT5 },
        { type : float4, name : camK5 },
        { type : float4, name : camDist5 },
        { type : float, name : camK3_5 },
        { type : float3, name : skyColor },
        { type : float, name : featherMargin },
        { type : float, name : exposureCompensation }
    ],
    requires : [ color, custom0 ],
    variables : [ custom0, custom2 ]
}
vertex {
    void materialVertex(inout MaterialVertexInputs material) {
        material.custom0 = material.color;
        material.custom2 = vec4(getCustom0().xyz, 0.0);
    }
}
fragment {
    void material(inout MaterialInputs material) {
        prepareMaterial(material);
        vec4 c0 = variable_custom0;
        vec3 rigPos = variable_custom2.xyz;
        float coverageA = c0.x;
        int idxA = int(c0.y + 0.5);
        float coverageB = c0.z;
        int idxB = int(c0.w + 0.5);

        vec3 colorSum = vec3(0.0);
        float wsum = 0.0;

        // -- camera 0 -- right/fwd/t are the EFFECTIVE (ego-motion-delta
        // -composed) extrinsics bowl.cpp uploads each render_frame call;
        // `down` is reconstructed as cross(fwd,right) rather than uploaded
        // (an orthonormal right-handed basis's third axis, exact -- see
        // bowl.mat's header for the parameter-budget reason). width/height
        // come from textureSize(), not a uniform. Feather (review round 1
        // blocking finding) is computed HERE, per fragment, from
        // featherMargin -- ported verbatim from blend.cuh's
        // border_feather/smoothstep01 -- not baked per-vertex, so the
        // border falls off smoothly instead of stepping hard at the
        // vertex-baked cutoff. UV (review round 1 minor finding) is
        // pixel-CENTER sampled (+0.5), matching reproject.cu's bilinear().
        {
            float coverage = (idxA == 0) ? coverageA : ((idxB == 0) ? coverageB : 0.0);
            if (coverage > 0.0) {
                vec3 fwd = materialParams.camFwd0;
                vec3 right = materialParams.camRight0;
                vec3 down = cross(fwd, right);
                vec3 rel = rigPos - materialParams.camT0;
                float zc = dot(fwd, rel);
                if (zc > 1e-9) {
                    float xn = dot(right, rel) / zc;
                    float yn = dot(down, rel) / zc;
                    float k1 = materialParams.camDist0.x;
                    float k2 = materialParams.camDist0.y;
                    float p1 = materialParams.camDist0.z;
                    float p2 = materialParams.camDist0.w;
                    float k3 = materialParams.camK3_0;
                    bool distorted = (k1 != 0.0 || k2 != 0.0 || p1 != 0.0 || p2 != 0.0 || k3 != 0.0);
                    float r2 = xn * xn + yn * yn;
                    bool inField = true;
                    if (distorted) {
                        if (r2 > 3.0) {
                            inField = false;
                        } else {
                            float radial = 1.0 + r2 * (k1 + r2 * (k2 + r2 * k3));
                            float xd = xn * radial + 2.0 * p1 * xn * yn + p2 * (r2 + 2.0 * xn * xn);
                            float yd = yn * radial + p1 * (r2 + 2.0 * yn * yn) + 2.0 * p2 * xn * yn;
                            xn = xd;
                            yn = yd;
                        }
                    }
                    if (inField) {
                        float fx = materialParams.camK0.x;
                        float fy = materialParams.camK0.y;
                        float cx = materialParams.camK0.z;
                        float cy = materialParams.camK0.w;
                        ivec2 dims = textureSize(materialParams_camTex0, 0);
                        float width = float(dims.x);
                        float height = float(dims.y);
                        float xp = fx * xn + cx;
                        float yp = fy * yn + cy;
                        if (xp >= 0.0 && xp <= width - 1.0 && yp >= 0.0 && yp <= height - 1.0) {
                            float d = min(min(xp, (width - 1.0) - xp), min(yp, (height - 1.0) - yp));
                            float feather;
                            if (materialParams.featherMargin <= 0.0) {
                                feather = step(0.0, d);
                            } else {
                                float ratio = clamp(d / materialParams.featherMargin, 0.0, 1.0);
                                feather = ratio * ratio * (3.0 - 2.0 * ratio);
                            }
                            float wgt = coverage * feather;
                            if (wgt > 0.0) {
                                vec2 uv = (vec2(xp, yp) + 0.5) / vec2(width, height);
                                colorSum += wgt * texture(materialParams_camTex0, uv).rgb;
                                wsum += wgt;
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        // -- camera 1 -- right/fwd/t are the EFFECTIVE (ego-motion-delta
        // -composed) extrinsics bowl.cpp uploads each render_frame call;
        // `down` is reconstructed as cross(fwd,right) rather than uploaded
        // (an orthonormal right-handed basis's third axis, exact -- see
        // bowl.mat's header for the parameter-budget reason). width/height
        // come from textureSize(), not a uniform. Feather (review round 1
        // blocking finding) is computed HERE, per fragment, from
        // featherMargin -- ported verbatim from blend.cuh's
        // border_feather/smoothstep01 -- not baked per-vertex, so the
        // border falls off smoothly instead of stepping hard at the
        // vertex-baked cutoff. UV (review round 1 minor finding) is
        // pixel-CENTER sampled (+0.5), matching reproject.cu's bilinear().
        {
            float coverage = (idxA == 1) ? coverageA : ((idxB == 1) ? coverageB : 0.0);
            if (coverage > 0.0) {
                vec3 fwd = materialParams.camFwd1;
                vec3 right = materialParams.camRight1;
                vec3 down = cross(fwd, right);
                vec3 rel = rigPos - materialParams.camT1;
                float zc = dot(fwd, rel);
                if (zc > 1e-9) {
                    float xn = dot(right, rel) / zc;
                    float yn = dot(down, rel) / zc;
                    float k1 = materialParams.camDist1.x;
                    float k2 = materialParams.camDist1.y;
                    float p1 = materialParams.camDist1.z;
                    float p2 = materialParams.camDist1.w;
                    float k3 = materialParams.camK3_1;
                    bool distorted = (k1 != 0.0 || k2 != 0.0 || p1 != 0.0 || p2 != 0.0 || k3 != 0.0);
                    float r2 = xn * xn + yn * yn;
                    bool inField = true;
                    if (distorted) {
                        if (r2 > 3.0) {
                            inField = false;
                        } else {
                            float radial = 1.0 + r2 * (k1 + r2 * (k2 + r2 * k3));
                            float xd = xn * radial + 2.0 * p1 * xn * yn + p2 * (r2 + 2.0 * xn * xn);
                            float yd = yn * radial + p1 * (r2 + 2.0 * yn * yn) + 2.0 * p2 * xn * yn;
                            xn = xd;
                            yn = yd;
                        }
                    }
                    if (inField) {
                        float fx = materialParams.camK1.x;
                        float fy = materialParams.camK1.y;
                        float cx = materialParams.camK1.z;
                        float cy = materialParams.camK1.w;
                        ivec2 dims = textureSize(materialParams_camTex1, 0);
                        float width = float(dims.x);
                        float height = float(dims.y);
                        float xp = fx * xn + cx;
                        float yp = fy * yn + cy;
                        if (xp >= 0.0 && xp <= width - 1.0 && yp >= 0.0 && yp <= height - 1.0) {
                            float d = min(min(xp, (width - 1.0) - xp), min(yp, (height - 1.0) - yp));
                            float feather;
                            if (materialParams.featherMargin <= 0.0) {
                                feather = step(0.0, d);
                            } else {
                                float ratio = clamp(d / materialParams.featherMargin, 0.0, 1.0);
                                feather = ratio * ratio * (3.0 - 2.0 * ratio);
                            }
                            float wgt = coverage * feather;
                            if (wgt > 0.0) {
                                vec2 uv = (vec2(xp, yp) + 0.5) / vec2(width, height);
                                colorSum += wgt * texture(materialParams_camTex1, uv).rgb;
                                wsum += wgt;
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        // -- camera 2 -- right/fwd/t are the EFFECTIVE (ego-motion-delta
        // -composed) extrinsics bowl.cpp uploads each render_frame call;
        // `down` is reconstructed as cross(fwd,right) rather than uploaded
        // (an orthonormal right-handed basis's third axis, exact -- see
        // bowl.mat's header for the parameter-budget reason). width/height
        // come from textureSize(), not a uniform. Feather (review round 1
        // blocking finding) is computed HERE, per fragment, from
        // featherMargin -- ported verbatim from blend.cuh's
        // border_feather/smoothstep01 -- not baked per-vertex, so the
        // border falls off smoothly instead of stepping hard at the
        // vertex-baked cutoff. UV (review round 1 minor finding) is
        // pixel-CENTER sampled (+0.5), matching reproject.cu's bilinear().
        {
            float coverage = (idxA == 2) ? coverageA : ((idxB == 2) ? coverageB : 0.0);
            if (coverage > 0.0) {
                vec3 fwd = materialParams.camFwd2;
                vec3 right = materialParams.camRight2;
                vec3 down = cross(fwd, right);
                vec3 rel = rigPos - materialParams.camT2;
                float zc = dot(fwd, rel);
                if (zc > 1e-9) {
                    float xn = dot(right, rel) / zc;
                    float yn = dot(down, rel) / zc;
                    float k1 = materialParams.camDist2.x;
                    float k2 = materialParams.camDist2.y;
                    float p1 = materialParams.camDist2.z;
                    float p2 = materialParams.camDist2.w;
                    float k3 = materialParams.camK3_2;
                    bool distorted = (k1 != 0.0 || k2 != 0.0 || p1 != 0.0 || p2 != 0.0 || k3 != 0.0);
                    float r2 = xn * xn + yn * yn;
                    bool inField = true;
                    if (distorted) {
                        if (r2 > 3.0) {
                            inField = false;
                        } else {
                            float radial = 1.0 + r2 * (k1 + r2 * (k2 + r2 * k3));
                            float xd = xn * radial + 2.0 * p1 * xn * yn + p2 * (r2 + 2.0 * xn * xn);
                            float yd = yn * radial + p1 * (r2 + 2.0 * yn * yn) + 2.0 * p2 * xn * yn;
                            xn = xd;
                            yn = yd;
                        }
                    }
                    if (inField) {
                        float fx = materialParams.camK2.x;
                        float fy = materialParams.camK2.y;
                        float cx = materialParams.camK2.z;
                        float cy = materialParams.camK2.w;
                        ivec2 dims = textureSize(materialParams_camTex2, 0);
                        float width = float(dims.x);
                        float height = float(dims.y);
                        float xp = fx * xn + cx;
                        float yp = fy * yn + cy;
                        if (xp >= 0.0 && xp <= width - 1.0 && yp >= 0.0 && yp <= height - 1.0) {
                            float d = min(min(xp, (width - 1.0) - xp), min(yp, (height - 1.0) - yp));
                            float feather;
                            if (materialParams.featherMargin <= 0.0) {
                                feather = step(0.0, d);
                            } else {
                                float ratio = clamp(d / materialParams.featherMargin, 0.0, 1.0);
                                feather = ratio * ratio * (3.0 - 2.0 * ratio);
                            }
                            float wgt = coverage * feather;
                            if (wgt > 0.0) {
                                vec2 uv = (vec2(xp, yp) + 0.5) / vec2(width, height);
                                colorSum += wgt * texture(materialParams_camTex2, uv).rgb;
                                wsum += wgt;
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        // -- camera 3 -- right/fwd/t are the EFFECTIVE (ego-motion-delta
        // -composed) extrinsics bowl.cpp uploads each render_frame call;
        // `down` is reconstructed as cross(fwd,right) rather than uploaded
        // (an orthonormal right-handed basis's third axis, exact -- see
        // bowl.mat's header for the parameter-budget reason). width/height
        // come from textureSize(), not a uniform. Feather (review round 1
        // blocking finding) is computed HERE, per fragment, from
        // featherMargin -- ported verbatim from blend.cuh's
        // border_feather/smoothstep01 -- not baked per-vertex, so the
        // border falls off smoothly instead of stepping hard at the
        // vertex-baked cutoff. UV (review round 1 minor finding) is
        // pixel-CENTER sampled (+0.5), matching reproject.cu's bilinear().
        {
            float coverage = (idxA == 3) ? coverageA : ((idxB == 3) ? coverageB : 0.0);
            if (coverage > 0.0) {
                vec3 fwd = materialParams.camFwd3;
                vec3 right = materialParams.camRight3;
                vec3 down = cross(fwd, right);
                vec3 rel = rigPos - materialParams.camT3;
                float zc = dot(fwd, rel);
                if (zc > 1e-9) {
                    float xn = dot(right, rel) / zc;
                    float yn = dot(down, rel) / zc;
                    float k1 = materialParams.camDist3.x;
                    float k2 = materialParams.camDist3.y;
                    float p1 = materialParams.camDist3.z;
                    float p2 = materialParams.camDist3.w;
                    float k3 = materialParams.camK3_3;
                    bool distorted = (k1 != 0.0 || k2 != 0.0 || p1 != 0.0 || p2 != 0.0 || k3 != 0.0);
                    float r2 = xn * xn + yn * yn;
                    bool inField = true;
                    if (distorted) {
                        if (r2 > 3.0) {
                            inField = false;
                        } else {
                            float radial = 1.0 + r2 * (k1 + r2 * (k2 + r2 * k3));
                            float xd = xn * radial + 2.0 * p1 * xn * yn + p2 * (r2 + 2.0 * xn * xn);
                            float yd = yn * radial + p1 * (r2 + 2.0 * yn * yn) + 2.0 * p2 * xn * yn;
                            xn = xd;
                            yn = yd;
                        }
                    }
                    if (inField) {
                        float fx = materialParams.camK3.x;
                        float fy = materialParams.camK3.y;
                        float cx = materialParams.camK3.z;
                        float cy = materialParams.camK3.w;
                        ivec2 dims = textureSize(materialParams_camTex3, 0);
                        float width = float(dims.x);
                        float height = float(dims.y);
                        float xp = fx * xn + cx;
                        float yp = fy * yn + cy;
                        if (xp >= 0.0 && xp <= width - 1.0 && yp >= 0.0 && yp <= height - 1.0) {
                            float d = min(min(xp, (width - 1.0) - xp), min(yp, (height - 1.0) - yp));
                            float feather;
                            if (materialParams.featherMargin <= 0.0) {
                                feather = step(0.0, d);
                            } else {
                                float ratio = clamp(d / materialParams.featherMargin, 0.0, 1.0);
                                feather = ratio * ratio * (3.0 - 2.0 * ratio);
                            }
                            float wgt = coverage * feather;
                            if (wgt > 0.0) {
                                vec2 uv = (vec2(xp, yp) + 0.5) / vec2(width, height);
                                colorSum += wgt * texture(materialParams_camTex3, uv).rgb;
                                wsum += wgt;
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        // -- camera 4 -- right/fwd/t are the EFFECTIVE (ego-motion-delta
        // -composed) extrinsics bowl.cpp uploads each render_frame call;
        // `down` is reconstructed as cross(fwd,right) rather than uploaded
        // (an orthonormal right-handed basis's third axis, exact -- see
        // bowl.mat's header for the parameter-budget reason). width/height
        // come from textureSize(), not a uniform. Feather (review round 1
        // blocking finding) is computed HERE, per fragment, from
        // featherMargin -- ported verbatim from blend.cuh's
        // border_feather/smoothstep01 -- not baked per-vertex, so the
        // border falls off smoothly instead of stepping hard at the
        // vertex-baked cutoff. UV (review round 1 minor finding) is
        // pixel-CENTER sampled (+0.5), matching reproject.cu's bilinear().
        {
            float coverage = (idxA == 4) ? coverageA : ((idxB == 4) ? coverageB : 0.0);
            if (coverage > 0.0) {
                vec3 fwd = materialParams.camFwd4;
                vec3 right = materialParams.camRight4;
                vec3 down = cross(fwd, right);
                vec3 rel = rigPos - materialParams.camT4;
                float zc = dot(fwd, rel);
                if (zc > 1e-9) {
                    float xn = dot(right, rel) / zc;
                    float yn = dot(down, rel) / zc;
                    float k1 = materialParams.camDist4.x;
                    float k2 = materialParams.camDist4.y;
                    float p1 = materialParams.camDist4.z;
                    float p2 = materialParams.camDist4.w;
                    float k3 = materialParams.camK3_4;
                    bool distorted = (k1 != 0.0 || k2 != 0.0 || p1 != 0.0 || p2 != 0.0 || k3 != 0.0);
                    float r2 = xn * xn + yn * yn;
                    bool inField = true;
                    if (distorted) {
                        if (r2 > 3.0) {
                            inField = false;
                        } else {
                            float radial = 1.0 + r2 * (k1 + r2 * (k2 + r2 * k3));
                            float xd = xn * radial + 2.0 * p1 * xn * yn + p2 * (r2 + 2.0 * xn * xn);
                            float yd = yn * radial + p1 * (r2 + 2.0 * yn * yn) + 2.0 * p2 * xn * yn;
                            xn = xd;
                            yn = yd;
                        }
                    }
                    if (inField) {
                        float fx = materialParams.camK4.x;
                        float fy = materialParams.camK4.y;
                        float cx = materialParams.camK4.z;
                        float cy = materialParams.camK4.w;
                        ivec2 dims = textureSize(materialParams_camTex4, 0);
                        float width = float(dims.x);
                        float height = float(dims.y);
                        float xp = fx * xn + cx;
                        float yp = fy * yn + cy;
                        if (xp >= 0.0 && xp <= width - 1.0 && yp >= 0.0 && yp <= height - 1.0) {
                            float d = min(min(xp, (width - 1.0) - xp), min(yp, (height - 1.0) - yp));
                            float feather;
                            if (materialParams.featherMargin <= 0.0) {
                                feather = step(0.0, d);
                            } else {
                                float ratio = clamp(d / materialParams.featherMargin, 0.0, 1.0);
                                feather = ratio * ratio * (3.0 - 2.0 * ratio);
                            }
                            float wgt = coverage * feather;
                            if (wgt > 0.0) {
                                vec2 uv = (vec2(xp, yp) + 0.5) / vec2(width, height);
                                colorSum += wgt * texture(materialParams_camTex4, uv).rgb;
                                wsum += wgt;
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        // -- camera 5 -- right/fwd/t are the EFFECTIVE (ego-motion-delta
        // -composed) extrinsics bowl.cpp uploads each render_frame call;
        // `down` is reconstructed as cross(fwd,right) rather than uploaded
        // (an orthonormal right-handed basis's third axis, exact -- see
        // bowl.mat's header for the parameter-budget reason). width/height
        // come from textureSize(), not a uniform. Feather (review round 1
        // blocking finding) is computed HERE, per fragment, from
        // featherMargin -- ported verbatim from blend.cuh's
        // border_feather/smoothstep01 -- not baked per-vertex, so the
        // border falls off smoothly instead of stepping hard at the
        // vertex-baked cutoff. UV (review round 1 minor finding) is
        // pixel-CENTER sampled (+0.5), matching reproject.cu's bilinear().
        {
            float coverage = (idxA == 5) ? coverageA : ((idxB == 5) ? coverageB : 0.0);
            if (coverage > 0.0) {
                vec3 fwd = materialParams.camFwd5;
                vec3 right = materialParams.camRight5;
                vec3 down = cross(fwd, right);
                vec3 rel = rigPos - materialParams.camT5;
                float zc = dot(fwd, rel);
                if (zc > 1e-9) {
                    float xn = dot(right, rel) / zc;
                    float yn = dot(down, rel) / zc;
                    float k1 = materialParams.camDist5.x;
                    float k2 = materialParams.camDist5.y;
                    float p1 = materialParams.camDist5.z;
                    float p2 = materialParams.camDist5.w;
                    float k3 = materialParams.camK3_5;
                    bool distorted = (k1 != 0.0 || k2 != 0.0 || p1 != 0.0 || p2 != 0.0 || k3 != 0.0);
                    float r2 = xn * xn + yn * yn;
                    bool inField = true;
                    if (distorted) {
                        if (r2 > 3.0) {
                            inField = false;
                        } else {
                            float radial = 1.0 + r2 * (k1 + r2 * (k2 + r2 * k3));
                            float xd = xn * radial + 2.0 * p1 * xn * yn + p2 * (r2 + 2.0 * xn * xn);
                            float yd = yn * radial + p1 * (r2 + 2.0 * yn * yn) + 2.0 * p2 * xn * yn;
                            xn = xd;
                            yn = yd;
                        }
                    }
                    if (inField) {
                        float fx = materialParams.camK5.x;
                        float fy = materialParams.camK5.y;
                        float cx = materialParams.camK5.z;
                        float cy = materialParams.camK5.w;
                        ivec2 dims = textureSize(materialParams_camTex5, 0);
                        float width = float(dims.x);
                        float height = float(dims.y);
                        float xp = fx * xn + cx;
                        float yp = fy * yn + cy;
                        if (xp >= 0.0 && xp <= width - 1.0 && yp >= 0.0 && yp <= height - 1.0) {
                            float d = min(min(xp, (width - 1.0) - xp), min(yp, (height - 1.0) - yp));
                            float feather;
                            if (materialParams.featherMargin <= 0.0) {
                                feather = step(0.0, d);
                            } else {
                                float ratio = clamp(d / materialParams.featherMargin, 0.0, 1.0);
                                feather = ratio * ratio * (3.0 - 2.0 * ratio);
                            }
                            float wgt = coverage * feather;
                            if (wgt > 0.0) {
                                vec2 uv = (vec2(xp, yp) + 0.5) / vec2(width, height);
                                colorSum += wgt * texture(materialParams_camTex5, uv).rgb;
                                wsum += wgt;
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        // EXPOSURE_COMPENSATION (materialParams.exposureCompensation, review
        // round 1 -- was a hardcoded shader constant): this renderer's fixed
        // camera exposure (renderer.cpp's setExposure(16, 1/500, 100), tuned
        // against SUN-lit clay surfaces) crushes an UNLIT material's raw
        // baseColor -- an unlit (1,1,1) renders at only ~15% output
        // brightness (measured empirically against this exact material, no
        // lighting to compensate the way clay.mat's albedo relies on the
        // sun). The CUDA reference (reproject.cu) writes camera RGB straight
        // to its output buffer with NO exposure/tonemap step at all, so
        // passing sampled camera pixels through unscaled would make the bowl
        // read as a dim, washed-out image compared to the CUDA node's own
        // output -- a real fidelity regression, not just a test-sentinel
        // artifact. 10.0x was picked empirically (matc/this build's tonemap
        // curve is nonlinear/saturating, so this is a working compensation,
        // not a precise inverse) to bring a well-lit camera pixel back into
        // a normal-looking display range; Task 2 Step 7's golden comparison
        // against the CUDA node's own output is the real check on whether
        // this constant needs retuning. skyColor is deliberately NOT
        // multiplied by it (see this material's header) -- sky_color is
        // authored in display space already, not the pre-tonemap camera-
        // pixel space exposureCompensation corrects for.
        if (wsum > 0.0) {
            material.baseColor.rgb = (colorSum / wsum) * materialParams.exposureCompensation;
        } else {
            material.baseColor.rgb = materialParams.skyColor;
        }
        material.baseColor.a = 1.0;
    }
}
